@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@
+domain: mobile_security
+version: 1.0
+description: >-
+  Hardware-rooted mobile device security (Android platform and Samsung Knox): boot chain,
+  rollback protection, app and process isolation, secure-world key custody, runtime kernel
+  integrity and remote attestation. Invariants carry source tags defined in
+  docs/DEEP_SYSTEM_INVARIANTS.md; failure modes and patterns are template-author mappings.
+components:
+  - name: hardware_root_of_trust
+    function: immutable boot ROM, fused public-key hash and device-unique key that software cannot rewrite or read directly
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: immune_system
+  - name: verified_boot_chain
+    function: each boot stage authenticates the next before handing off control
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: immune_system
+  - name: rollback_counter
+    function: monotonic index or fuse that rejects older images
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: vaccination
+  - name: kernel_runtime_monitor
+    function: guards kernel code, page tables and credentials from a more privileged level than the kernel
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: immune_system
+  - name: app_sandbox
+    function: per-app UID isolation plus mandatory access control for every process
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: quarantine
+  - name: secure_world
+    function: separate execution environment for keys and authentication, isolated by hardware and software
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: quarantine
+  - name: key_custody
+    function: holds key material inside the secure environment so callers use keys but cannot export them
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: quarantine
+  - name: user_auth_gate
+    function: verifies PIN, pattern or password with rate limiting and exponential backoff
+    criticality: medium
+    medical_map: homeostasis
+  - name: integrity_attestation
+    function: returns signed, nonce-bound evidence of device state that chains to a vendor root
+    criticality: medium
+    medical_map: diagnosis
+  - name: tamper_ledger
+    function: one-way fuse recording that an unapproved configuration ever ran
+    criticality: medium
+    medical_map: diagnosis
+relationships:
+  - from: hardware_root_of_trust
+    to: verified_boot_chain
+    type: anchors
+  - from: rollback_counter
+    to: verified_boot_chain
+    type: constrains
+  - from: verified_boot_chain
+    to: kernel_runtime_monitor
+    type: hands_off_to
+  - from: kernel_runtime_monitor
+    to: app_sandbox
+    type: guards_kernel_beneath
+  - from: secure_world
+    to: key_custody
+    type: hosts
+  - from: secure_world
+    to: user_auth_gate
+    type: hosts
+  - from: user_auth_gate
+    to: key_custody
+    type: gates_release_of
+  - from: hardware_root_of_trust
+    to: integrity_attestation
+    type: roots_signature_chain_of
+  - from: verified_boot_chain
+    to: tamper_ledger
+    type: records_deviation_in
+  - from: tamper_ledger
+    to: key_custody
+    type: revokes_access_to
+invariants:
+  - "verification starts at a hardware-protected root of trust and every boot stage verifies the next before handing off control [AOSP-VB][KNOX-WP]"
+  - "the root of trust's public key lives in one-time-programmable fuses and the device-unique key is reachable only by a hardware crypto module, never directly by software [KNOX-WP]"
+  - "boot terminates when signature verification fails at any step of the secure-boot chain, and strict enforcement means a verification failure blocks boot [KNOX-WP][AOSP-VB]"
+  - "a bootable but unapproved configuration is recorded permanently and the device-bound keys it gates stop working, instead of being silently tolerated [KNOX-WP]"
+  - "older images are rejected: rollback protection and irreversible rollback fuses stop a device being downgraded to a vulnerable version [AOSP-VB][KNOX-WP]"
+  - "each app runs in its own sandbox under a unique UID and must be signed by its developer [AOSP-SEC]"
+  - "mandatory access control (SELinux) applies to every process, including root [AOSP-SEC]"
+  - "the system partition is mounted read-only [AOSP-SEC]"
+  - "dm-verity checks the integrity of verified partitions, and forward error correction addresses non-malicious corruption as a reliability measure, not a security one [AOSP-VB]"
+  - "key material stays inside the secure environment: keys are used there and not exported, and they are encrypted with a vault-unique key so they cannot be decrypted on another device [AOSP-SEC][KNOX-WP]"
+  - "secure-world memory and peripherals are reachable only from the secure world [KNOX-WP]"
+  - "repeated secret guessing is rate limited, with exponential backoff on failed reads [AOSP-SEC][KNOX-WP]"
+  - "physical tamper detection wipes protected storage automatically [KNOX-WP]"
+  - "kernel integrity is enforced from a more privileged level than the kernel: page-table changes happen only in the secure world, kernel code pages are never writable, kernel data pages are never executable, user pages are never executable by the kernel, and process credentials are read-only to the normal world [KW-2016]"
+  - "attestation evidence is bound to a server-issued nonce to prevent replay and chains from a device attestation key through a vendor attestation key to the vendor root key [KNOX-WP]"
+  - "platform protections depend on kernel integrity, because a kernel bug that yields root can bypass them [AOSP-SEC]"
+failure_modes:
+  - name: root_of_trust_compromise
+    medical_map: sepsis
+    description: a flaw in the boot ROM or a leaked signing key lets every later stage trust unverified code
+    indicators: [leaked_signing_key, boot_rom_flaw, unverified_stage_executes]
+  - name: downgrade_to_vulnerable_image
+    medical_map: pathogen
+    description: an older but correctly signed image is accepted and reintroduces a known vulnerability
+    indicators: [older_signed_image_accepted, rollback_index_not_advanced, rollback_fuse_unblown]
+  - name: kernel_privilege_escalation
+    medical_map: metastasis
+    description: a kernel write primitive turns one compromised process into control of the whole device
+    indicators: [kernel_write_primitive, credential_structure_modified, mandatory_access_control_disabled_at_runtime]
+  - name: monitor_trusts_monitored_state
+    medical_map: autoimmune
+    description: the integrity monitor depends on a key or input generated in the domain it is meant to police
+    indicators: [monitor_key_generated_in_normal_world, monitor_inputs_unauthenticated]
+  - name: container_shared_service_leak
+    medical_map: pathogen
+    description: isolation between containers leaks through shared services such as a certificate store or clipboard
+    indicators: [shared_certificate_store, shared_clipboard, cross_container_data_read]
+  - name: verification_coverage_gap
+    medical_map: chronic
+    description: part of the system sits outside verification, so an unverified component persists below trusted layers
+    indicators: [optional_partition_unverified, unsigned_component_loaded]
+  - name: stale_attestation_accepted
+    medical_map: pathogen
+    description: replayed or unbound attestation evidence gives the verifier a wrong picture of the device
+    indicators: [reused_nonce, missing_nonce, stale_timestamp]
+architecture_patterns:
+  - name: verified_boot_chain
+    medical_map: immune_system
+    description: every stage authenticates its successor, rooted in hardware
+  - name: privilege_separation_by_hardware
+    medical_map: quarantine
+    description: secure world and hypervisor isolate keys and monitors from the normal-world kernel
+  - name: anti_rollback_counter
+    medical_map: vaccination
+    description: monotonic index or fuse closes known-vulnerable versions before they can be reinstalled
+  - name: exponential_backoff_on_secrets
+    medical_map: homeostasis
+    description: failed secret reads slow down so guessing stays outside a safe operating range
+  - name: monotonic_tamper_record
+    medical_map: diagnosis
+    description: a permanent fuse records deviation so later checks and key release can depend on it
+  - name: runtime_monitor_from_higher_privilege
+    medical_map: immune_system
+    description: critical kernel actions are intercepted by a component the kernel cannot modify
+  - name: remote_attestation
+    medical_map: diagnosis
+    description: signed, nonce-bound device state lets a remote party check health before trusting the device
