+++ b/expansion/templates/poe_chaos_inoculation.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@
+domain: poe_chaos_inoculation
+version: 1.0
+description: >-
+  Single-buffer defense in Path of Exile (PoE 1 and PoE 2): the Chaos Inoculation keystone sets
+  maximum life to 1 and grants immunity to chaos damage, so survival rests on an energy shield
+  buffer, a regulated recharge, converted recovery and a closed bypass channel. These are
+  designed game rules, versioned by patch; the template preserves their structure, not their
+  numbers. Invariants carry source tags defined in docs/POE_CHAOS_INOCULATION_INVARIANTS.md and
+  name the game version they were sourced for (PoE 1, PoE 2 or both); failure modes and patterns are template-author
+  mappings.
+components:
+  - name: chaos_inoculation_keystone
+    function: one indivisible trade that sets maximum life to 1 and grants immunity to chaos damage
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: vaccination
+  - name: lethal_pool
+    function: the life pool whose depletion is death, reduced to a constant of 1 so any damage reaching it is fatal
+    criticality: high
+  - name: energy_shield_pool
+    function: the buffer that absorbs damage before it can reach the lethal pool
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: immune_system
+  - name: damage_ordering_rule
+    function: routes damage to the buffer first and to the lethal pool only after the buffer is depleted, except for damage that bypasses the buffer
+    criticality: high
+  - name: chaos_immunity
+    function: full immunity to chaos damage, the damage type that ignores the buffer
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: vaccination
+  - name: recharge_regulator
+    function: refills the buffer only during quiet time (a period with no damage taken) and restarts the delay whenever damage lands, so refill depends on the gaps between hits rather than on elapsed time
+    criticality: high
+    medical_map: homeostasis
+  - name: recovery_converters
+    function: turn life-based recovery (leech, regeneration, flask recovery) into buffer recovery because the life pool is only 1; unlike recharge it does not wait for quiet time
+    criticality: medium
+    medical_map: treatment
+  - name: threshold_calculator
+    function: derives stun and ailment thresholds from life before the override to 1, so life modifiers still scale them
+    criticality: medium
+    medical_map: prognosis
+  - name: excluded_subsystems
+    function: mechanics that need a life pool and stop working, such as low-life effects, life flasks and life-cost skills
+    criticality: medium
+    medical_map: quarantine
+relationships:
+  - from: chaos_inoculation_keystone
+    to: lethal_pool
+    type: sets_to_one
+  - from: chaos_inoculation_keystone
+    to: chaos_immunity
+    type: grants
+  - from: chaos_inoculation_keystone
+    to: excluded_subsystems
+    type: disables
+  - from: chaos_inoculation_keystone
+    to: threshold_calculator
+    type: leaves_life_basis_to
+  - from: damage_ordering_rule
+    to: energy_shield_pool
+    type: routes_damage_first_to
+  - from: energy_shield_pool
+    to: lethal_pool
+    type: protects
+  - from: chaos_immunity
+    to: damage_ordering_rule
+    type: closes_bypass_of
+  - from: recharge_regulator
+    to: energy_shield_pool
+    type: refills
+  - from: recovery_converters
+    to: energy_shield_pool
+    type: feeds
+invariants:
+  - "the keystone is one trade: maximum life becomes 1 and the character becomes immune to chaos damage, with neither half available alone (PoE 1 and PoE 2) [POEDB-CI][MOBA-ES]"
+  - "damage is dealt to energy shield first and reaches life only once energy shield is depleted, with bypass exceptions (PoE 1 and PoE 2) [FANDOM-ES][MOBA-ES]"
+  - "chaos damage ignores energy shield in PoE 1, so a character whose only life is 1 is exposed to it unless it is immune [FANDOM-ES][FANDOM-EB][POEDB-CI]"
+  - "in PoE 2 (January 2025 guide) chaos damage removes twice as much energy shield, and poison and bleeding damage skip energy shield and hit life directly [MOBA-ES]"
+  - "in PoE 2 (January 2025 guide) a hit must deal damage to life to inflict bleeding, so an intact buffer blocks it, and chaos immunity leaves poison with no damage to deal [MOBA-ES]"
